# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Windows checks out text files as CRLF (core.autocrlf defaults
# to true there) and those carriage returns flow straight through the build
# into dist-offline/index.html. Measured on the 2026-08-03 cross-platform
# matrix run: Linux and macOS produced byte-identical artefacts, while Windows
# differed by exactly 70 bytes — the first at char 16, the newline after
# <!DOCTYPE html>.
#
# That matters because RELEASE.md asks users to rebuild the offline artefact
# and compare its SHA-256 against the published one. A checkout-time newline
# rewrite makes that check fail on a genuine artefact, which trains people to
# ignore mismatches — the one signal that would indicate a real compromise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary content.
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute on the runner.
*.sh    text eol=lf

